  "content": {
    "id": "p41-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Find all solutions of $2\\cos\\theta=\\sqrt{3}\\cot\\theta$ for $0\\leq\\theta\\leq2\\pi$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{3},\\dfrac{\\pi}{2},\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3},\\dfrac{3\\pi}{2}$.",
      "worked": "Since $\\cot\\theta=\\dfrac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}$, the original equation requires $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$.\n\nCheck $\\cos\\theta=0$ separately: $\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2},\\dfrac{3\\pi}{2}$. Both give $0=0$ in the original equation.\n\nFor $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$, divide by $\\cos\\theta$:\n$$\\begin{align*}2&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sin\\theta}\\\\2\\sin\\theta&=\\sqrt{3}\\\\\\sin\\theta&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\frac{2\\pi}{3}.\\end{align*}$$\nThus all solutions are $\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{3},\\dfrac{\\pi}{2},\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3},\\dfrac{3\\pi}{2}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 42
